\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Star1\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"9\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Star1_fd1ea6.png\" width=\"10\"/></span><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Star1\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"9\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Star1_fd1ea6.png\" width=\"10\"/></span></p></td>\n<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"loot\"><p style=\"text-align: center; color: green\"><b>Good</b></p><p style=\"text-align: center; margin: 0.4em 0 0.5em;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Star1\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"9\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Star1_fd1ea6.png\" width=\"10\"/></span><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Star1\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"9\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Star1_fd1ea6.png\" width=\"10\"/></span><br/><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Star1\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"9\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Star1_fd1ea6.png\" width=\"10\"/></span><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Star1\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"9\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Star1_fd1ea6.png\" width=\"10\"/></span></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Other Properties</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"implemented\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"implementation-date\">8.00<br/>June 26, 2007<br/>Summer Update 2007</span></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><p>\t    See also: Hunting Places <span class=\"explained\">Help</span></p></nav>\n</aside>\n<p>The <b>Barbarian Settlements</b> are located south-west of <a href=\"#/wiki/Svargrond\">Svargrond</a>. There are three settlements, named after the major clans of raiders: <a href=\"#/wiki/Ragnir\">Ragnir</a> (located in an inactive volcano), <a href=\"#/wiki/Bittermor\">Bittermor</a> (located under the glacier) and <a href=\"#/wiki/Krimhorn\">Krimhorn</a> (located on a peninsula).\n</p><p>You can travel to these fields talking with <a href=\"#/wiki/Buddel\">Buddel</a>, asking for <b>passage</b>, then <b>raider camp</b> and confirm the answer. There is a chance he will take you to a different island, but the chances are lower after a patch. You can also reach the settlements by walking through the glacier and a small bridge to the west of <a href=\"#/wiki/Svargrond\">Svargrond</a> - it is a faster and cheaper way of getting there.\n</p><p>These settlements are profitable when you're talking about Loot. <a href=\"#/wiki/Barbarians\">Barbarians</a> drop lots of addon items and you can get some <a href=\"#/wiki/Tusk\">Tusks</a>, <a href=\"#/wiki/Bear%20Paw\">Bear Paws</a> and Furry Clubs when you're trying to avoid <a href=\"#/wiki/Mammoth\">Mammoths</a> and <a href=\"#/wiki/Polar%20Bear\">Polar Bears</a>.\n</p><p>Bordering these 3 settlements, the glacier Formorgar hosts countless animals like <a href=\"#/wiki/Mammoth\">Mammoths</a> and <a href=\"#/wiki/Polar%20Bear\">Polar Bears</a> and dangerous and fierce creatures such as <a href=\"#/wiki/Ice%20Golem\">Ice Golems</a> and <a href=\"#/wiki/Crystal%20Spider\">Crystal Spiders</a>. Deep under the glacier, a strange cult has set up their camp in an old mine. It is rumoured that they are melting ancient demons there, hoping to be able to conjure a mighty archdemon one day.\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Creatures\">Creatures</span></h2>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div><table cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable full-width\"><caption>Settlements Creatures</caption><tbody><tr><th>Name</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"width: 38px; text-align: center;\">Exp</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\"